"""Boann's own version: one number for the whole engine family (the shared Metal/CPU machinery and
every solver: ACC, SGC, FV1, FV2, DG2, sub-grid FV, sub-grid local inertial), separate from the Runner's and Screening's.

Bump it when anything in this folder changes what a run computes or what the command line accepts
(minor for a new solver, option or output; patch for a fix; major when an existing result moves).
The Runner records it in the run manifest (software.boann) beside its own version.

Each solver module still carries its own NAME / VERSION, written as the first line of the
lisflood.log a run leaves; those are unchanged."""
BOANN_VERSION = "6.11.0"   # 6.11.0 (DamSafety Core 1.11.0): the OpenCL backend stops copying the whole model state every batch - a GPU that shares the computer's memory (integrated: Intel Arc/Iris, AMD APU, a CPU OpenCL) holds each grid zero-copy over host memory (CL_MEM_USE_HOST_PTR, mapped/unmapped per batch, as Metal's shared storage), and a discrete GPU reads a grid back only the first time the engine looks it up and uploads only the grids it touched (no shadow); DAMSAFETY_MF_CL_ZEROCOPY and DAMSAFETY_MF_CL_SYNC=full switch it; results byte-identical, no result moves; 6.10.0 (DamSafety Core 1.10.0): the OpenCL backend now runs sub-grid FV too (kernels_subfv.metal translates - its one reference out-param, which OpenCL C has no form for, became a float* pointer, valid in Metal and OpenCL alike and a no-op for the result; --backend opencl works for every solver now; auto never picks it, no result moves); 6.9.1 (DamSafety Core 1.9.1): a Windows CPU build compiled with MinGW-w64 g++ links statically (-static) so Python can open it, and a built library that does not open is rebuilt (no result moves); 6.9.0 (DamSafety Core 1.9.0): opt-in OpenCL backend for GPUs that are not Apple's (Intel Arc, AMD, NVIDIA; --backend opencl, opencl_backend.py: the .metal kernels translated to OpenCL C; ACC, SGC, FV1, FV2, DG2, sub-grid local inertial; auto never picks it, no result moves); 6.8.1 (DamSafety Core 1.8.1): a Windows install runs the shipped CPU libraries - the source hash in a library's name ignores line ends (a Git for Windows CRLF checkout matched no prebuilt library), BoannGrid's available() and bench.py count a prebuilt library as well as a compiler, bench.py makes its --out folder (no result moves); 6.8.0 (Runner 3.103.0, DamSafety Core 1.8.0): water-level (stage) boundary, LISFLOOD-FP's HFIX / HVAR .bci edge lines, in ACC, FV1, FV2 and DG2 (new input; a deck without one is byte-identical; SGC, sub-grid FV and sub-grid local inertial refuse a deck with one); 6.7.0 (Runner 3.102.0): FV1, FV2 and DG2 skip dry tiles on the GPU (16 x 16; FV1 a 1-tile ring every 8 steps, FV2 and DG2 a 1-tile ring every 4 steps; no result moves); 6.6.1 (Runner 3.101.1, DamSafety Core 1.7.0): one copy - Boann moves from the Runner's core/metalflood + core/metalterrain to DamSafety_Core/boann/hydro + grid, Screening's subset copy is gone (no result moves: every result file byte-identical); 6.6.0 (Runner 3.100.0): opt-in notch lowered into the bed (.bed, .pool; the breach cells' .mxe is the peak over time of depth + the lowering bed; a resumed run keeps its stable settings; the no-breach baseline stays intact; a batch crest line is used when the dam has none; .pool times never go backwards); off, no existing result moves; 6.5.0 (Runner 3.99.0): peak depth x velocity grid (.maxDV; total water depth times speed at one moment, not depth above the arrival depth and not shifted by the breach-initiation time); new output, no existing result moves; 6.4.0 (Runner 3.98.0): FV1 adds rain on the grid, the same source term as the ACC engine (LISFLOOD-FP's "rainfall" keyword; new input, no existing result moves; FV2/DG2 still refuse rain); 6.3.1 (Runner 3.97.1): after the first tile redraw of a batch, a tile that was off is not scanned again (ACC and sub-grid local inertial; no result moves); 6.3.0 (Runner 3.97.0): the sub-grid local-inertial engine skips dry tiles on the Apple GPU (no result moves); 6.0.1 (Runner 3.96.0): result grids' text written about 7x faster, the same bytes (no result moves); 6.0.0 (Runner 3.93.0): FV1, FV2 and DG2 make a face against NoData a reflecting wall (FV1/FV2/DG2 results move where water reaches NoData); 5.5.0 (Runner 3.90.0): the ACC engine skips dry tiles on the Apple GPU (DAMSAFETY_MF_TILES; no result moves); 5.4.1 (Runner 3.89.0): Mac CPU build defaults to the performance cores (no result moves); 5.4.0 (Runner 3.80.0): the profile (--profile, stats["profile"]; no result moves); 5.3.0 (Runner 3.79.0): new solver, sub-grid local inertial (gpu-subli; no existing result moves); 5.1.1 (Runner 3.76.0): CPU build skips dry cells, OpenMP on a Mac (no result moves); 5.1.0 (Runner 3.75.0): rain on the grid (ACC; new input); 5.0.0 (Runner 3.68.0): sub-grid FV positivity limiter (sub-grid FV results move); 4.0.0 (Runner 3.67.0): DG2 primitive edge velocities (DG2 results move)
